---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import { DOC_SECTIONS, docRoute } from "../lib/navigation";
---

<Base title="eBrain | Persistent memory for coding agents" description="The relevant memory arrives with every prompt, in the agents you already use, and secrets stay out of the conversation.">
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main-content" class="home">
    <section class="home-intro" aria-labelledby="home-title">
      <div class="home-intro__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Persistent memory for coding agents</p>
        <h1 id="home-title">eBrain</h1>
        <p class="home-intro__lede">The memory arrives with the prompt. Secrets stay out.</p>
        <p>Agents almost never ask a memory tool for anything: in one month of real use, the tools were called 0 times, while context injected by a hook reached 20 of 31 sessions. eBrain puts the relevant, current documents into each prompt through the hook every agent already has, and denies the reads that would send a credential to the model provider.</p>
        <div class="home-intro__links" aria-label="Start here">
          <a href={docRoute("getting-started/quickstart")}>Follow the quick start <img src="/icons/arrow-right.svg" alt="" width="16" height="16" /></a>
          <a href="/docs/">Open documentation</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="local-proof" aria-labelledby="local-proof-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Install and check</p>
        <h2 id="local-proof-title">One command, then verify what each agent really reads.</h2>
      </div>
      <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aedneth/ebrain/main/scripts/install.sh | sh
ebrain doctor
ebrain harness install codex
ebrain harness doctor codex</code></pre>
      <p>Linux only is claimed. Codex, Antigravity and Hermes are wired and checked; the others are declared but not verified in this release. To switch the memory off in every agent: <code>{'touch "${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/ebrain/sin-memoria-en-prompt"'}</code>.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="docs-paths" aria-labelledby="docs-paths-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What it does, and what it does not</p>
        <h2 id="docs-paths-title">Measured, with the method stated.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="docs-paths__grid">
        {[
          { title: "Memory in each prompt", body: "In a 44-case retrieval regression run the way a hook runs it, the current document was in the injected text in 73 % of the cases (68 % as a result of its own), and no archived, retired or client document was injected. One private brain, one command: the README states the method.", href: docRoute("concepts/memory") },
          { title: "A guard that covers file tools", body: "One canonical guard for shell reads, plus a translator so agents that read files with their own tools cannot bypass it.", href: docRoute("guides/agents") },
          { title: "Verified against the agent", body: "The doctor fails when a hook file sits where the agent does not look, and asks the agent itself where it can.", href: docRoute("guides/agents") },
          { title: "What it does not do", body: "No retrieval command ships for your brain, a clean install has nothing to search yet, and think and synthesize are off on purpose.", href: docRoute("getting-started/quickstart") },
        ].map((path) => (
          <a class="path-link" href={path.href}>
            <h3>{path.title}</h3>
            <p>{path.body}</p>
            <span>Read <img src="/icons/arrow-right.svg" alt="" width="16" height="16" /></span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="docs-catalog" aria-labelledby="docs-catalog-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Documentation</p>
        <h2 id="docs-catalog-title">Every page below was checked against the code.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="docs-catalog__columns">
        {DOC_SECTIONS.map((section) => (
          <section>
            <h3>{section.title}</h3>
            <ul>
              {section.links.map((doc) => <li><a href={docRoute(doc.id)}>{doc.title}</a></li>)}
            </ul>
          </section>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
